---
mm: 1.1
kind: app
name: mdy
use: mm.app
use: mm.mdy
use: mm.build
file: mdy.cpp
option: buildable-target no
---

# mdy application

Reads an MDY document and renders it as HTML. Given a kind:project or kind:dir manifest it walks the whole tree instead, writing one page per manifest, which is what document.sh runs.

buildable-target no because document.sh runs this application on the build
machine to render the manifests; unlike apps/main it is a host tool that happens
to live under apps.
